  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I am now in a situation regarding my internet connection where the public IP used by my desktop PC changes from day-to-day between two different values. It's always the same two, but it periodically changes from one to the other. This change invalidates my session in the VRC client and forces me to enter credentials again, despite having used VRC from that IP before.\n\nNo other application on my computer does this. I do not see any valid reason for VRC to be special here - I launch it through Steam and Steam never invalidates my session like this. It is annoying typing any relatively strong password on a VR keyboard, or trying to operate a password manager from a VR overlay.",
